### Health & operational endpoints (S15)
# These live at the ROOT (not /api/v1), are anonymous, and are excluded from the OpenAPI document.
# They are for orchestrators and load balancers, not partners.

@host = http://localhost:5000

### Liveness — is the process alive? Checks nothing downstream. Expect 200 {"status":"live"} always.
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Liveness with a caller-supplied correlation id — it is echoed back on X-Correlation-Id.
GET {{host}}/health/live
X-Correlation-Id: my-trace-0001

### Readiness — should this node receive traffic? Gated on the DB; outbox lag is reported, not gated.
# Expect 200 when healthy:
# {
#   "status": "ready",
#   "checks": [
#     { "name": "database",          "status": "ok", "detail": "reachable" },
#     { "name": "outbox-dispatcher", "status": "ok", "detail": "pending=0, oldestDueAgeSeconds=0, poisoned=0" }
#   ]
# }
# When the dispatcher is behind, the outbox line reads "status":"degraded" but the overall status
# stays "ready" (200) — lag pages an operator, it does not drain the node. See ADR-0018.
# When the database is unreachable, the whole response is 503 with "status":"not-ready" and the
# database line reads "status":"down".
GET {{host}}/health/ready
